  - partName: Arytenoid cartilage.l
    systemName: Visceral Systems
    partType: Cartilaginous Structure
    description: "A specialized internal visceral structure (Arytenoid cartilage) organized with specialized parenchymal and epithelial tissues designed for systemic physiological processes."
    function: "Performs vital metabolic, filtration, digestive, endocrine, or respiratory activities essential for systemic physiological homeostasis."
    location: "Situated within the protective cavity of the cervical (neck) region. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
