  - partName: Atlas (C1)
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Atlas (C1)) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Axis (C2)
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Axis (C2)) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Body of sternum
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: "The sternum (breastbone) is a flat, elongated plate located in the anterior thoracic midline. It is composed of three fused segments - the superior pentagonal manubrium, the elongated central body (mesosternum), and the inferior cartilaginous xiphoid process."
    function: "Protects the vital mediastinal organs (heart and great vessels), articulates with true costal cartilages (ribs 1–7) to facilitate respiratory chest expansion, and anchors pectoral muscles."
    location: "Forms the anterior midline anchor of the thoracic cage, articulating laterally with the bilateral clavicles and ribs 1 through 7. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma7487"
    fmaPreferredName: Body of sternum
  - partName: Calcaneus.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Short Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Calcaneus) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the ankle (talocrural region). Left side (bilateral structure)."
