    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Clavicle.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The clavicle (collarbone) is an elongated S-shaped bone that forms the anterior portion of the shoulder girdle. It features a rounded medial sternal end, flattened lateral acromial end, and conoid tubercle."
    function: "Acts as a rigid mechanical strut that suspends the scapula and upper limb away from the thoracic wall, maximizing rotational freedom and transferring impact loads to the axial skeleton."
    location: "Extends horizontally across the superior anterior thorax between the sternal manubrium medially and the scapular acromion laterally. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Clavicle.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The clavicle (collarbone) is an elongated S-shaped bone that forms the anterior portion of the shoulder girdle. It features a rounded medial sternal end, flattened lateral acromial end, and conoid tubercle."
