    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Femur.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The femur (thigh bone) is the longest, heaviest, and strongest tubular bone in the human body. It comprises a proximal femoral head with fovea capitis, anatomical neck, greater and lesser trochanters, an anteriorly bowed shaft, and distal medial and lateral condyles."
    function: "Transmits the entirety of upper body weight to the lower leg during upright bipedal stance and ambulation; serves as the primary mechanical lever arm for the powerful hip and knee muscle groups."
    location: "Extends through the thigh compartment, articulating proximally with the pelvic acetabulum (hip joint) and distally with the tibia and patella (knee joint). Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Femur.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The femur (thigh bone) is the longest, heaviest, and strongest tubular bone in the human body. It comprises a proximal femoral head with fovea capitis, anatomical neck, greater and lesser trochanters, an anteriorly bowed shaft, and distal medial and lateral condyles."
    function: "Transmits the entirety of upper body weight to the lower leg during upright bipedal stance and ambulation; serves as the primary mechanical lever arm for the powerful hip and knee muscle groups."
    location: "Extends through the thigh compartment, articulating proximally with the pelvic acetabulum (hip joint) and distally with the tibia and patella (knee joint). Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fibula.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The fibula is the slender, non-weight-bearing lateral bone of the leg. It features an expanded proximal head with an articular facet, a slender grooved shaft, and a pyramidal distal expansion known as the lateral malleolus."
    function: "Provides extensive attachment area for leg and ankle eversion/inversion muscles and forms the lateral retaining wall of the ankle mortise joint to prevent lateral talar subluxation."
    location: "Runs parallel and lateral to the tibia in the lower leg, bound tightly along its length by the interosseous membrane. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fibula.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The fibula is the slender, non-weight-bearing lateral bone of the leg. It features an expanded proximal head with an articular facet, a slender grooved shaft, and a pyramidal distal expansion known as the lateral malleolus."
    function: "Provides extensive attachment area for leg and ankle eversion/inversion muscles and forms the lateral retaining wall of the ankle mortise joint to prevent lateral talar subluxation."
    location: "Runs parallel and lateral to the tibia in the lower leg, bound tightly along its length by the interosseous membrane. Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
