  - partName: Humerus.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The humerus is the principal long bone of the upper arm. It features a hemispherical proximal head, anatomical and surgical necks, greater and lesser tubercles, deltoid tuberosity, radial groove, and distal capitulum, trochlea, and medial/lateral epicondyles."
    function: "Provides rigid structural support for the upper arm, acts as the primary skeletal lever for shoulder and elbow kinematics, and anchors 24 muscular attachments."
    location: "Occupies the brachial region of the upper limb; articulates proximally with the glenoid cavity of the scapula and distally with the radius and ulna at the elbow. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Humerus.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The humerus is the principal long bone of the upper arm. It features a hemispherical proximal head, anatomical and surgical necks, greater and lesser tubercles, deltoid tuberosity, radial groove, and distal capitulum, trochlea, and medial/lateral epicondyles."
    function: "Provides rigid structural support for the upper arm, acts as the primary skeletal lever for shoulder and elbow kinematics, and anchors 24 muscular attachments."
    location: "Occupies the brachial region of the upper limb; articulates proximally with the glenoid cavity of the scapula and distally with the radius and ulna at the elbow. Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Hyoid bone
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Hyoid bone) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the cervical (neck) region. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma52749"
    fmaPreferredName: Hyoid bone
