  - partName: Patella.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Sesamoid Bone
    description: "The patella (kneecap) is the largest sesamoid bone in the human skeleton, situated within the common tendon of the quadriceps femoris. Its posterior surface is coated with the thickest hyaline cartilage in the human body (up to 6mm)."
    function: "Displaces the quadriceps tendon anteriorly away from the knee joint axis, increasing the mechanical extensor lever arm by up to 30% and shielding the joint from direct frontal trauma."
    location: "Positioned anterior to the distal femoral trochlea, gliding within the intercondylar sulcus during knee flexion and extension. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
