    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the wrist (carpal region). Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Scapula.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: "The scapula (shoulder blade) is a broad, triangular flat bone positioned on the posterolateral thorax. It presents a prominent dorsal spine terminating in the acromion, a coracoid process, supraspinous/infraspinous fossae, and a glenoid cavity."
    function: "Provides the mobile foundational platform for upper extremity articulation via scapulothoracic gliding and anchors 17 distinct muscles, including the four rotator cuff stabilizers."
    location: "Overlies posterior ribs 2 through 7; articulates laterally with the humeral head at the glenohumeral joint and with the clavicle at the acromioclavicular joint. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
