  - partName: Thyroid cartilage
    systemName: Visceral Systems
    partType: Cartilaginous Structure
    description: "A specialized internal visceral structure (Thyroid cartilage) organized with specialized parenchymal and epithelial tissues designed for systemic physiological processes."
    function: "Performs vital metabolic, filtration, digestive, endocrine, or respiratory activities essential for systemic physiological homeostasis."
    location: "Situated within the protective cavity of the cervical (neck) region. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma55099"
    fmaPreferredName: Thyroid cartilage
  - partName: Tibia.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The tibia (shin bone) is the massive, weight-bearing medial bone of the lower leg. It possesses an expanded proximal tibial plateau with medial/lateral condyles, a prominent anterior tibial tuberosity, a prismatic triangular shaft, and distal medial malleolus."
    function: "Bears approximately 85-90% of the body weight transmitted through the lower extremity, enabling stable standing, running, and jumping."
    location: "Located anteromedially in the lower leg; articulates proximally with the femoral condyles and distally with the talus and fibula. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
