  - partName: Ulna.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "The ulna is the medial stabilizing long bone of the forearm. Its massive proximal end displays the hook-like olecranon, coronoid process, and trochlear notch, tapering distally to a small rounded head and styloid process."
    function: "Forms the primary structural hinge of the elbow joint with the humeral trochlea, restricting joint kinematics strictly to sagittal flexion and extension."
    location: "Located medially in the forearm; articulates proximally with the trochlea of the humerus and distally with the triangular fibrocartilage complex (TFCC). Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: Ulna Length in Black Children
