    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Irregular Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Vertebra L5) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the vertebral column and posterior torso. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
