  - partName: Xiphoid process
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Landmark / Feature
    description: "A prominent osseous projection and morphological landmark (Xiphoid process) formed on the cortical surface of the parent bone."
    function: "Expands mechanical surface area for the strong anchorage of tendons and ligaments, enhancing biomechanical lever arms and distributing joint stresses."
    location: "Projecting from the surface of the bone in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma7488"
    fmaPreferredName: Xiphoid process
