  - partName: Zygomatic bone.r
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Zygomatic bone) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
