    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Abductor digiti minimi of foot.el
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscular Insertion
    description: "Represents the anatomical insertion (distal/mobile attachment enthesis) of the Abductor digiti minimi of foot. At this site, the muscle's terminal tendon or aponeurosis fuses with the cortical bone matrix."
    function: "Transfers tensile muscular contraction forces directly onto the articulated bone, driving joint rotation, leverage, and biomechanical limb displacement."
    location: "Located at the distal bony insertion site within the hand and digits. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
