  - partName: Longus capitis muscle.ol
    systemName: Muscular Insertions
    partType: Muscular Origin
    description: "Represents the anatomical origin (proximal/immobile anchoring enthesis) of the Longus capitis muscle. It consists of dense fibrous connective tissue and Sharpey's fibers interdigitating with the periosteum of the underlying bone."
    function: "Secures the proximal tendon of the Longus capitis muscle firmly to skeletal bone, providing a stable mechanical base that absorbs reaction forces during dynamic muscular contraction."
    location: "Located at the proximal bony origin site within the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
