    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Abdominal aorta
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Artery
    description: "The aorta is the primary and largest systemic artery in the body, emerging directly from the left ventricle. It is anatomically subdivided into the ascending aorta, aortic arch, descending thoracic aorta, and abdominal aorta."
    function: "Transports oxygenated blood at peak systolic pressure from the left ventricle into the systemic arterial branches feeding all peripheral organ systems."
    location: "Arises from the base of the heart, arches superiorly over the pulmonary trunk in the superior mediastinum, and descends anterior to the spine into the abdomen. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma3789"
    fmaPreferredName: Abdominal aorta
  - partName: Coeliac trunk
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Coeliac trunk) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Common hepatic artery
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Artery
    description: "A high-pressure arterial vessel (Common hepatic artery) composed of three concentric histological layers - tunica intima, media (smooth muscle and elastin), and adventitia."
    function: "Distributes pulsatile oxygenated blood and essential metabolic nutrients to the tissues, skeletal muscles, and viscera of the abdominal cavity and anterior abdominal wall."
    location: "Courses along the neurovascular plane of the abdominal cavity and anterior abdominal wall. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma14771"
    fmaPreferredName: Common hepatic artery
  - partName: Gastroduodenal artery
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Artery
    description: "A high-pressure arterial vessel (Gastroduodenal artery) composed of three concentric histological layers - tunica intima, media (smooth muscle and elastin), and adventitia."
    function: "Distributes pulsatile oxygenated blood and essential metabolic nutrients to the tissues, skeletal muscles, and viscera of the human body."
    location: "Courses along the neurovascular plane of the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma14775"
    fmaPreferredName: Gastroduodenal artery
