  - partName: Intrarenal arteries of left kidney
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Artery
    description: "The kidney is a bean-shaped retroperitoneal organ featuring an outer renal cortex containing over one million nephrons and an inner medulla organized into renal pyramids that drain into minor and major calyces and the renal pelvis."
    function: "Ultrafilters circulating blood plasma to remove metabolic wastes (urea, creatinine), maintains electrolyte and fluid balance, regulates blood pH, controls systemic arterial pressure via the renin-angiotensin system, and secretes erythropoietin."
    location: "Retroperitoneal on the posterior abdominal wall on either side of the vertebral column between T12 and L3; the right kidney sits slightly lower due to liver displacement."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
