  - partName: Ascending aorta
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Artery
    description: "The aorta is the primary and largest systemic artery in the body, emerging directly from the left ventricle. It is anatomically subdivided into the ascending aorta, aortic arch, descending thoracic aorta, and abdominal aorta."
    function: "Transports oxygenated blood at peak systolic pressure from the left ventricle into the systemic arterial branches feeding all peripheral organ systems."
    location: "Arises from the base of the heart, arches superiorly over the pulmonary trunk in the superior mediastinum, and descends anterior to the spine into the abdomen. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma3736"
    fmaPreferredName: Ascending aorta
