  - partName: Coronary sinus
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Vascular Structure
    description: "A recognized topographical and clinical surface landmark of the human body (Coronary sinus), serving as a primary surgical and diagnostic reference space."
    function: "Defines clinical anatomical boundaries, encapsulates underlying neurovascular bundles, and provides external landmarks for physical palpation and surgical approaches."
    location: "Situated within the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
