  - partName: ????????
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (????????) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Great cardiac vein
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Vein
    description: "A low-pressure capacitance blood vessel (Great cardiac vein) featuring thin muscular walls and intraluminal bicuspid valves designed to promote unidirectional hemodynamic return."
    function: "Collects deoxygenated blood and metabolic waste products from the microcirculation of the human body, funneling it back toward the heart and vena cava."
    location: "Courses through the superficial and deep venous fascia of the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma4707"
    fmaPreferredName: Great cardiac vein
