  - partName: Left coronary leaflet
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Vascular Structure
    description: "A recognized topographical and clinical surface landmark of the human body (coronary leaflet), serving as a primary surgical and diagnostic reference space."
    function: "Defines clinical anatomical boundaries, encapsulates underlying neurovascular bundles, and provides external landmarks for physical palpation and surgical approaches."
    location: "Situated within the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Left inferior pulmonary vein
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Vein
    description: "A low-pressure capacitance blood vessel (inferior pulmonary vein) featuring thin muscular walls and intraluminal bicuspid valves designed to promote unidirectional hemodynamic return."
    function: "Collects deoxygenated blood and metabolic waste products from the microcirculation of the thoracic (chest) cavity and thoracic wall, funneling it back toward the heart and vena cava."
    location: "Courses through the superficial and deep venous fascia of the thoracic (chest) cavity and thoracic wall. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma49913"
    fmaPreferredName: Left inferior pulmonary vein
