  - partName: Non-coronary leaflet
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Vascular Structure
    description: "A recognized topographical and clinical surface landmark of the human body (Non coronary leaflet), serving as a primary surgical and diagnostic reference space."
    function: "Defines clinical anatomical boundaries, encapsulates underlying neurovascular bundles, and provides external landmarks for physical palpation and surgical approaches."
    location: "Situated within the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Occipital sinus
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Flat Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Occipital sinus) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the head and cranial region. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma50781"
    fmaPreferredName: Occipital sinus
