    description: "A low-pressure capacitance blood vessel (brachiocephalic vein) featuring thin muscular walls and intraluminal bicuspid valves designed to promote unidirectional hemodynamic return."
    function: "Collects deoxygenated blood and metabolic waste products from the microcirculation of the human body, funneling it back toward the heart and vena cava."
    location: "Courses through the superficial and deep venous fascia of the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma4761"
    fmaPreferredName: Left brachiocephalic vein
