  - partName: (Abdominal part of pectoralis major muscle).l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: "A voluntary skeletal muscle (Abdominal part of pectoralis major muscle) formed by organized fascicles of multinucleated striated muscle fibers enclosed by the epimysium."
    function: "Generates active tensile force through actin-myosin cross-bridge cycling to stabilize articulated joints, power limb movement, and maintain upright body posture."
    location: "Situated within the muscular compartment of the thoracic (chest) cavity and thoracic wall. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: (Abdominal part of pectoralis major muscle).r
    systemName: Muscular System
