  - partName: Acromial part of deltoid muscle.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: "The deltoid is a thick, multipennate muscle cap that drapes over the glenohumeral joint. It arises from the lateral third of the clavicle, acromion, and scapular spine, converging distally to insert onto the deltoid tuberosity of the humerus."
    function: "The central acromial fibers are the primary motor for arm abduction between 15° and 90°; the anterior clavicular fibers flex and medially rotate the arm; the posterior spinal fibers extend and laterally rotate the arm."
    location: "Forms the prominent rounded contour of the shoulder; innervated by the axillary nerve (C5, C6). Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
