    systemName: Visceral Systems
    partType: Visceral Organ
    description: "A specialized internal visceral structure (Diaphragmatic fascia) organized with specialized parenchymal and epithelial tissues designed for systemic physiological processes."
    function: "Performs vital metabolic, filtration, digestive, endocrine, or respiratory activities essential for systemic physiological homeostasis."
    location: "Situated within the protective cavity of the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
