  - partName: Epicranial aponeurosis.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Tendon / Aponeurosis
    description: "A dense regular connective tissue sheet or tendon (Epicranial aponeurosis) composed of densely bundled parallel collagen fibers engineered to withstand strong mechanical tension."
    function: "Anchors muscle bellies to the skeletal framework, stabilizes the underlying fascia, and transmits muscular kinetic forces across wide anatomical regions."
    location: "Extends across the fascial plane within the head and cranial region. Left side (bilateral structure)."
