  - partName: Inferior subtendinous bursa of biceps femoris muscle.l
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Synovial Bursa
    description: "An articulated junction (Inferior subtendinous bursa of biceps femoris muscle) where adjacent skeletal elements meet, lined with smooth articular hyaline cartilage and enclosed by a synovial fluid-filled capsule."
    function: "Permits controlled mechanical degrees of freedom (flexion, extension, rotation, or gliding) while distributing biomechanical compressive loads."
    location: "Positioned between articulating bones in the arm (brachial region). Left side (bilateral structure)."
