    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Lateral femoral intermuscular septum) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the thigh compartment. Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
