    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Short head of biceps brachii.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: "The biceps brachii is a prominent two-headed fusiform muscle of the anterior arm. It originates via a short head from the coracoid process and a long head from the supraglenoid tubercle, converging to insert onto the radial tuberosity."
    function: "Acts as the most powerful supinator of the flexed forearm, a primary flexor of the elbow joint, and an accessory stabilizer of the glenohumeral joint."
    location: "Occupies the anterior compartment of the arm, superficial to the brachialis and coracobrachialis muscles; innervated by the musculocutaneous nerve (C5, C6). Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
