  - partName: Subtendinous bursa of triceps brachii muscle.l
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Synovial Bursa
    description: "The triceps brachii is a powerful three-headed muscle that spans nearly the entire posterior arm. Its long head arises from the infraglenoid tubercle, lateral head from the postero-lateral humerus, and medial head from the postero-medial humerus, inserting onto the olecranon."
    function: "Serves as the primary and most potent extensor of the elbow joint; the long head additionally assists in adduction and extension of the humerus at the shoulder."
    location: "Occupies the posterior compartment of the arm; innervated by multiple motor branches of the radial nerve (C6, C7, C8). Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
