  - partName: Superficial head of flexor pollicis brevis.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: "A voluntary skeletal muscle (Superficial head of flexor pollicis brevis) formed by organized fascicles of multinucleated striated muscle fibers enclosed by the epimysium."
    function: "Generates active tensile force through actin-myosin cross-bridge cycling to stabilize articulated joints, power limb movement, and maintain upright body posture."
