  - partName: Tendon sheath - abd. pollicis longus - ext. pollicis brevis.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Tendon / Aponeurosis
    description: "A dense regular connective tissue sheet or tendon (Tendon sheath abd. pollicis longus ext. pollicis brevis) composed of densely bundled parallel collagen fibers engineered to withstand strong mechanical tension."
    function: "Anchors muscle bellies to the skeletal framework, stabilizes the underlying fascia, and transmits muscular kinetic forces across wide anatomical regions."
    location: "Extends across the fascial plane within the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
