  - partName: Iliotibial tract.l
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Long Bone
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Iliotibial tract) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the lower leg (crural region). Left side (bilateral structure)."
