  - partName: Lesser omentum
    systemName: Regions & Surface Anatomy
    partType: Topographical Region
    description: "A recognized topographical and clinical surface landmark of the human body (Lesser omentum), serving as a primary surgical and diagnostic reference space."
    function: "Defines clinical anatomical boundaries, encapsulates underlying neurovascular bundles, and provides external landmarks for physical palpation and surgical approaches."
    location: "Situated within the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma9715"
    fmaPreferredName: Lesser omentum
  - partName: Liver
    systemName: Visceral Systems
    partType: Vital Organ
    description: "The liver (hepar) is the largest internal solid organ and metabolic gland in the human body, weighing approximately 1.5 kg. It is partitioned into right, left, caudate, and quadrate anatomical lobes, receiving dual blood supply from the portal vein and hepatic artery."
    function: "Executes over 500 vital biochemical functions - synthesizes bile, plasma albumins, and clotting factors; detoxifies endogenous and exogenous compounds; metabolizes carbohydrates, lipids, and amino acids; stores glycogen, iron, and vitamins."
    location: "Fills the right hypochondriac, epigastric, and part of the left hypochondriac regions of the abdomen, nestled directly beneath the right hemidiaphragm. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma7197"
    fmaPreferredName: Liver
  - partName: Caudate lobe.t
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Caudate lobe.t) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Caudate process.t
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Landmark / Feature
    description: "A prominent osseous projection and morphological landmark (Caudate process.t) formed on the cortical surface of the parent bone."
    function: "Expands mechanical surface area for the strong anchorage of tendons and ligaments, enhancing biomechanical lever arms and distributing joint stresses."
    location: "Projecting from the surface of the bone in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fissure for ligamentum teres.t
    systemName: Regions & Surface Anatomy
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Fissure for ligamentum teres.t) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Fissure for ligamentum venosum.t
    systemName: Regions & Surface Anatomy
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Fissure for ligamentum venosum.t) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Main portal fissure.t
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Foramen / Canal
    description: "An anatomical aperture or osseous passageway (Main portal fissure.t) penetrating through the bone structure."
    function: "Provides a protected anatomical transit channel through which neurovascular bundles (arteries, veins, and nerves) travel between body compartments."
    location: "Traversing the osseous framework of the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
