  - partName: Choroid plexus.l
    systemName: Cardiovascular System
    partType: Neural Plexus / Ganglion
    description: "A complex, highly anastomotic network of interconnected blood vessels (Choroid plexus) that lines and cushions neighboring structures."
    function: "Facilitates extensive collateral circulatory pathways, stabilizes local vascular pressures, and drains venous return from neighboring osseous and soft tissues."
    location: "Situated along the vascular bed within the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
