  - partName: Corpus callosum
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Nervous Tissue
    description: "A peripheral neural cable (Corpus callosum) composed of myelinated and unmyelinated nerve fibers bundled into fascicles by endoneurium, perineurium, and epineurium."
    function: "Conducts bidirectional electrophysiological signals - relays motor impulses from the spinal cord to target muscles and sensory feedback (proprioception, pain, temperature) back to the central nervous system."
    location: "Courses within the neurovascular bundle of the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma86464"
    fmaPreferredName: Corpus callosum
