  - partName: Pons.l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Central Nervous System Structure
    description: "A peripheral neural cable (Pons) composed of myelinated and unmyelinated nerve fibers bundled into fascicles by endoneurium, perineurium, and epineurium."
    function: "Conducts bidirectional electrophysiological signals - relays motor impulses from the spinal cord to target muscles and sensory feedback (proprioception, pain, temperature) back to the central nervous system."
    location: "Courses within the neurovascular bundle of the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
