  - partName: Sciatic nerve.l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Peripheral Nerve
    description: "The sciatic nerve is the largest and thickest nerve trunk in the human body (up to 2cm wide). Arising from the sacral plexus (L4-S3), it travels through the greater sciatic foramen into the posterior thigh, bifurcating into the tibial and common fibular nerves."
    function: "Provides motor innervation to the hamstring muscles, adductor magnus, and all lower leg and foot musculature; delivers sensory perception from the posterior leg, lateral ankle, and entire sole of the foot."
    location: "Emerges below the piriformis muscle in the buttock, courses down the midline of the posterior thigh beneath the biceps femoris into the popliteal fossa. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
