  - partName: Suspensory ligament of eyeball.l
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Suspensory ligament of eyeball) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the head and cranial region. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
