  - partName: Tonsil of cerebellum.l
    systemName: Lymphoid Organs
    partType: Central Nervous System Structure
    description: "An encapsulated lymphoid organ (Tonsil of cerebellum) packed with lymphocytes, macrophages, and dendritic cells organized into lymphoid follicles."
    function: "Filters extracellular lymph fluid or blood, phagocytoses cellular debris and foreign pathogens, and initiates adaptive immune responses."
    location: "Located along the lymphatic drainage channels of the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
