  - partName: Vestibulocochlear nerve (VIII).l
    systemName: Nervous System
    partType: Cranial Nerve
    description: "A specialized cranial nerve trunk (Vestibulocochlear nerve (VIII)) arising directly from the brainstem and emerging through cranial base foramina to innervate peripheral cranial structures."
    function: "Delivers somatic sensory, motor, or autonomic parasympathetic innervation to the head, neck, and upper visceral organs."
    location: "Originates from the brainstem and emerges through the base of the skull in the head and cranial region. Left side (bilateral structure)."
