    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Cartilaginous Structure
    description: "An articulated junction (Glenoid labrum) where adjacent skeletal elements meet, lined with smooth articular hyaline cartilage and enclosed by a synovial fluid-filled capsule."
    function: "Permits controlled mechanical degrees of freedom (flexion, extension, rotation, or gliding) while distributing biomechanical compressive loads."
    location: "Positioned between articulating bones in the human body. Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Iliolumbar ligament.l
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Iliolumbar ligament) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the vertebral column and posterior torso. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
