  - partName: Intra-articular ligament of head of rib
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Intra articular ligament of head of rib) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the head and cranial region. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma8962"
    fmaPreferredName: Intra-articular ligament of head of rib
