    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Nucleus pulposus T12 L1) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Oblique cord.l
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
    description: "A voluntary skeletal muscle (Oblique cord) formed by organized fascicles of multinucleated striated muscle fibers enclosed by the epimysium."
    function: "Generates active tensile force through actin-myosin cross-bridge cycling to stabilize articulated joints, power limb movement, and maintain upright body posture."
    location: "Situated within the muscular compartment of the human body. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Oblique cord.r
    systemName: Muscular System
    partType: Skeletal Muscle
