    location: "Situated within the muscular compartment of the human body. Right side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Oblique popliteal ligament.l
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Oblique popliteal ligament) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the knee joint and popliteal fossa. Left side (bilateral structure)."
    fmaId: 
