  - partName: Pubic symphysis
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Structure
    description: "An articulated junction (Pubic symphysis) where adjacent skeletal elements meet, lined with smooth articular hyaline cartilage and enclosed by a synovial fluid-filled capsule."
    function: "Permits controlled mechanical degrees of freedom (flexion, extension, rotation, or gliding) while distributing biomechanical compressive loads."
    location: "Positioned between articulating bones in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma16950"
    fmaPreferredName: Pubic symphysis
  - partName: Inferior pubic ligament
    systemName: Joints & Articulations
    partType: Articular Ligament
    description: "A tough, flexible band of dense fibrous connective tissue (Inferior pubic ligament) that connects adjacent bones across an anatomical joint."
    function: "Provides passive mechanical constraint, limits excessive joint translation and rotation, and houses mechanoreceptors for proprioceptive joint feedback."
    location: "Spans across the articular capsule of the joint in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
  - partName: Interpubic disc
    systemName: Skeletal System
    partType: Bony Structure
    description: "A rigid skeletal organ (Interpubic disc) constructed from an outer dense cortical bone layer, internal spongy trabecular cancellous bone, periosteum, and bone marrow."
    function: "Provides structural body scaffolding, mechanical lever arms for muscle action, hematopoiesis (blood cell production), and a systemic metabolic reservoir for calcium and phosphate."
    location: "Constitutes an integral part of the skeletal framework in the human body. Midline anatomical structure on the central body axis."
    fmaId: 
    fmaPreferredName: 
